From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:25:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gpl: end on Nesterov's iterate, not on its look-ahead
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each Nesterov iteration takes a gradient step from the look-ahead v_k to
the iterate u_(k+1) (nextCoordi_), then extrapolates the next
look-ahead, v_(k+1) = u_(k+1) + c_k (u_(k+1) - u_k) (nextSLPCoordi_),
with c_k = (a_k - 1) / a_(k+1) about 0.994 by iteration 500. The
density, the overflow and the HPWL are measured at v, the convergence
test reads that overflow, and updateDb() writes the gcells' density
centers, which are v. A run therefore ends one momentum step past the
placement the descent reached, with that step's wirelength on top. The
extrapolation also spreads the cells, so v is usually what crosses the
target overflow first, and the stop lands wherever the cells' motion
happens to be.

On a synthetic design (20,000 cells, utilization 0.05, target density
0.6) v's HPWL is 13 to 39 % above u's for the 222 iterations before the
stop; it ended 0.7 % above u because the step length happened to be cut
in the last three, while another design of the same kind ended 16 %
above. On gpl's regression designs v is 0.0 to 2.3 % above u at the
stop.

Once the look-ahead is within 1.25 times the target overflow,
NesterovBase::settleOnIterate() measures the iterate's overflow, and
convergence is judged by that. When it is at the target, the region
moves onto its iterate: the look-ahead is set to it, and the bins, pins,
overflow and HPWL are the iterate's. The run converges there, so the
placement written, the final table row, the trace's last entry and
routability's pass at the target overflow (GPL-0124) all describe the
iterate. No step is taken from a settled region, so its gradients are
left as they were: it converges in that iteration, unless a revert later
in it (routability, divergence) replaces its state with a snapshot's.

Until the region settles, the unscaled overflow is the iterate's while
the bins, the scaled overflow and the HPWL stay the look-ahead's, which
the next step and the penalty schedule are computed from. Whatever
compares the overflow with the target must read the iterate's, so that
it reads at the target only once the region sits on it; the others read
it next to the look-ahead's HPWL, one momentum step apart. The header
says so, with the two places a reader sees it: the row printed every 10
iterations shows the look-ahead's overflow, and a run that stops at its
iteration limit inside the window reports the iterate's.

Runs converge 0 to 3 iterations later, at an overflow at or below the
target as before, so every placement moves. Of gpl's tests, the 30
golden-log ones that change move by 0 to 2 iterations and -0.52 to
+0.02 % HPWL, the 11 :large_tests by 0 to 3 iterations and -0.05 to
-2.19 % (macro03 3.903 M -> 3.818 M um), and every other placement that
runs 30 iterations or more by -0.33 to +0.00 % (incremental03, which
diverges by design, +0.43 %). Placements that stop within 25 iterations,
tiny designs that start near the target overflow, move either way, -19 %
to +9 % (known_answer_test, place_ios_test's few-cell cases): that early
in a descent the momentum step shortens the wires as often as it
lengthens them. Their .ok and .defok files are not updated here (the
:large_tests logs already differ from them before this change).

The window is there because the two differ by one momentum step. While
the cells spread, the look-ahead is the further spread of the two and
usually reaches the target first (at the stop of 149 synthetic runs, the
iterate's overflow was the higher in 131), and the run ends on the
iterate 0 to 3 iterations later. XiangShan's XSTile
parent ends that way too, in a burst: in its five placements in two
builds the look-ahead's overflow falls 2 to 5 times faster in the last
iterations while its HPWL rises 3 to 47 %. There the iterate one or more
iterations later is further into the burst, and whether ending on it
saves wire is not measured. Only when the cells run away while the
overflow stalls does the look-ahead overshoot into full bins and the
iterate get there first: on a synthetic 1 M-cell design placed on
2048 x 2048 bins (HPWL +23 % in 15 iterations from overflow 0.11) the
iterate reaches 0.0992 at iteration 896 while the look-ahead is at
0.1071, and the run ends there at 134.8 M um. This change does not stop
a runaway; a momentum restart does.

Tests:
- end_of_descent_test places gcd from the core's center (355
  iterations). ConvergedPlacementIsTheIterate pins the iterate with a
  twin of the run, stopped by its iteration limit after the run's last
  iteration (target overflow 0, so nothing converges or settles), and
  checks the placement is that iterate and not its look-ahead;
  TraceEndsOnTheIterate checks the last row's HPWL is the twin's
  iterate's. Without this change the placement sits 569 DBU from the
  iterate and within 1 DBU of the look-ahead, and the last row reads
  the look-ahead's 5,193,967 DBU instead of the iterate's 5,190,358.
- routability_minimum_test FirstPassAtTargetIsTheIterate: a region that
  settles on its iterate at the target, with a settle wait open, runs
  pass 1 there (GPL-0124); a phase whose minimum is that pass ends on it
  (GPL-0125) with the density on the iterate and converges. With the
  look-ahead left where it was when the region settles, the phase ends
  with 317 gcells' density on the look-ahead.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that has it.

